# Skulk (CR 702.118b): Furtive Homunculus, a 2/1, attacking cannot be blocked by Bot2's Wicker Witch, a 3/1 (power one
# greater than its own: refusal), but can by Alpha Myr, a 2/1 (power equal to its own), and by Memnite, a 1/1 (the positive
# controls: both block, so each may). The Homunculus takes 2 + 1 damage and dies; Bot2 takes none.
# Bot1 casts it on turn 1 (Black Lotus); Bot2 casts its blockers on turn 2 (Black Lotus for the Witch, Moxen Jet and Pearl
# for Alpha Myr, Memnite for free).

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Furtive Homunculus
Island x22

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Wicker Witch
Alpha Myr
Memnite
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Furtive Homunculus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot2.Hand.Wicker Witch.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Alpha Myr.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Furtive Homunculus > Bot2)
! Bot2.Block(Wicker Witch > Furtive Homunculus)
Bot2.Block(Alpha Myr > Furtive Homunculus; Memnite > Furtive Homunculus)
? Combat.Blocks.Count = 2
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Graveyard = Furtive Homunculus; Black Lotus
